From 4e66d1f31bc7897456dcd1653efd14a91b94ac36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naveen S <quic_naves@quicinc.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Sep 2024 11:30:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sigma_dut: Restructure the bring up of config files

Currently the hostapd config files are getting
swapped when the interfaces are trying to come
up. For instance, if 2GHz and 5GHz are trying
to bring up, 2GHz should come up in link0 and
5GHz should come up in link1, but it is vice
versa when the vaps are brought up via sigma
as there is a swap in links and hostapd config
files bring up.

Restructred the code to bring up the hostapd
config files as per the order in which the user
expects and using the restructured link specific
variables.

Signed-off-by: Dhanavandhana Kannan <quic_dhanavan@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Naveen S <quic_naves@quicinc.com>
